**/*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Generated regression-report output, all three --report-format renderers
# (batch notebooks / static HTML / interactive HTML, each with its own raw
# funnel-comparison CSV trace data) -- reproducible from a regression run via
# ModCheck's regression_testing.py, not a stored baseline. Mirrors ModCheck's
# own .gitignore for the same content. Restore any of them with
# restore_reports.py; Testing/Resources/ReferenceResults/ IS the stored
# baseline and stays tracked.
Testing/Resources/Notebooks/
Testing/Resources/HtmlReports/
Testing/Resources/InteractiveReports/

# Nightly cron daemon's own logs and PID file -- see nightly_regression_cron.py.
Testing/Resources/CronLogs/

# Per-case regression run artifacts. The suite is driven one case per process for
# restart resilience -- see run_baseline.sh -- which leaves a log per case, a resume
# state file, and a report directory per run. All of it is reproducible:
# restore_reports.py re-renders any report from ReferenceResults/, which IS the stored
# baseline and stays tracked.
#
# These are GLOBS on purpose. This block used to enumerate one session's filenames, so
# the next session's names (HtmlReports_after*, after2_*, elsewhen_*, newcases_*) were
# not covered, and 158 untracked files plus 1.8 GB of generated reports accumulated
# before anyone noticed. Name a run whatever you like; it will be ignored.
Testing/Resources/HtmlReports_*/
Testing/Resources/*.log
Testing/Resources/_*.txt
Testing/Resources/_*.json
Testing/Resources/_probe*.py
Testing/Resources/_worksession/

# Pre-re-store copies of references. Belt-and-braces only: the previous versions of
# these tracked .npz are already recoverable from git history.
Testing/Resources/ReferenceResults_backup_*/
